### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### CeView · Module 4 · FastAPI Test Requests
### Requires: "REST Client" VS Code extension  (ritwickdey.rest-client)
### Run each request with the  ▶ Send Request  button that appears above it.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@base = http://localhost:8000

# ─── Health check ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1 · Health check — verify FastAPI is running
GET {{base}}/healthz HTTP/1.1


# ─── UC-4.2 / UC-4.3 · PES Compute from Raw Data ─────────────────────────────

### 2 · Happy-path: all metrics computable (no flags)
# Expected: pes_score ≈ 0.56, pes_label "Good Performance"
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-compute/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "impressions":  150000,
  "clicks":       7200,
  "adSpend":      5000.00,
  "revenue":      16000.00,
  "conversions":  350,
  "bookings":     180,
  "newCustomers": 80
}


### 3 · Edge case: newCustomers = 0  →  CAC flagged & excluded
# Expected: flagged_metrics contains "CAC (newCustomers = 0)"
#           effective_weights recalibrated to 4 metrics (sum = 1.0)
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-compute/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "impressions":  150000,
  "clicks":       7200,
  "adSpend":      5000.00,
  "revenue":      16000.00,
  "conversions":  350,
  "bookings":     180,
  "newCustomers": 0
}


### 4 · Edge case: clicks = 0  →  CPC, CR, CTR all flagged
# Expected: flagged_metrics has 3 entries; effective_weights only ROAS + CAC
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-compute/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "impressions":  100000,
  "clicks":       0,
  "adSpend":      3000.00,
  "revenue":      9000.00,
  "conversions":  0,
  "bookings":     0,
  "newCustomers": 20
}


### 5 · Edge case: all zeros (worst-case input)
# Expected: all metrics flagged, pes_score = 0.0, pes_label "Poor Performance"
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-compute/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "impressions":  0,
  "clicks":       0,
  "adSpend":      0,
  "revenue":      0,
  "conversions":  0,
  "bookings":     0,
  "newCustomers": 0
}


### 6 · Excellent performance test (high ROAS, high CR, low CPC, low CAC)
# Expected: pes_score ≥ 0.80, pes_label "Excellent Performance"
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-compute/analyze HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "impressions":  500000,
  "clicks":       50000,
  "adSpend":      10000.00,
  "revenue":      80000.00,
  "conversions":  8000,
  "bookings":     4000,
  "newCustomers": 3500
}


# ─── PES Time-Series Deep Analysis (LangGraph agent) ──────────────────────────

### 7 · PES analysis agent — 4-week time-series
# Expected: report_data with metric_conditions, cross_metric_logic, ranked_weaknesses
POST {{base}}/internal/pes-analysis/generate HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "metrics_data": {
    "CTR":  [4.8, 4.5, 4.2, 3.9],
    "CPC":  [0.72, 0.75, 0.81, 0.89],
    "ROAS": [5.4, 5.1, 4.8, 4.3],
    "CR":   [3.2, 3.0, 2.7, 2.5],
    "CAC":  [18.5, 19.8, 21.4, 24.0]
  },
  "weeks": 4
}


# ─── Prescriptive Report (Gemini / DeepSeek AI) ────────────────────────────────

### 8 · Prescriptive report — full funnel diagnostics
POST {{base}}/internal/report/generate HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "metrics": {
    "impressions":  150000,
    "clicks":       7200,
    "adSpend":      5000.00,
    "revenue":      16000.00,
    "conversions":  350,
    "bookings":     180,
    "newCustomers": 80
  },
  "funnelTransitions": [
    { "stage": "Clicks → Conversions",  "dropRate": "95.1%" },
    { "stage": "Conversions → Bookings","dropRate": "48.6%" },
    { "stage": "Impressions → Clicks",  "dropRate": "95.2%" }
  ],
  "weeks": 4,
  "market": "korea"
}
